gy manager**. Fill in the dictionary `MEMO` in the next cell. Every value is checked by the marking computer; nothing is read by a person. Use your own numbers, with at least two decimals, in **kVarh**.\\n\", \"\\n\", \"| Field | What to enter | Marks |\\n\", \"|---|---|---|\\n\", \"| `recommended_model` | One of the models you trained (`\\\"baseline\\\"`, `\\\"linear\\\"`, `\\\"tree\\\"`). It must be the model the supplied rule chose and the model you opened the test set with. | 3 |\\n\", \"| `validation_mae` | The validation MAE of each of the three models, as your notebook computed them. | 3 |\\n\", \"| `test_mae`, `test_recall` | The MAE and the warning recall on the test set from your ONE opening (recall is between 0 and 1). The marking computer recomputes them from your own functions. | 2 |\\n\", \"| `improvement_over_baseline` | The validation MAE of the baseline model minus the validation MAE of your recommended model, in kVarh (0 if you recommend the baseline). | 1 |\\n\", \"| `limits` | The letters of the **three** statements below that are **true limits of this study**. Three different letters. One mark for each true one. | 3 |\\n\", \"| `next_step` | One letter: the best next step. | 1 |\\n\", \"| `answer_choice`, `answer_test_set` | Two short written answers of 8 to 80 words each. One mark each. | 2 |\\n\", \"\\n\", \"**Limits.** Choose the three statements that are TRUE and are limits of this study (some statements are false):\\n\", \"- **A.** The test set is only November and December of the same year, so the test metrics are one estimate that may be luckier or unluckier than the truth.\\n\", \"- **B.** The model with the lowest training error is always the best model for new months.\\n\", \"- **C.** The client limits (the error limit and the time limit) and the warning limit are invented teaching numbers; a real client would set their own.\\n\", \"- **D.** The baseline model should be left out of the comparison because it uses no features.\\n\", \"- **E.** Because the test set was opened only once, the test metrics have no uncertainty at all.\\n\", \"- **F.** All the readings come from one steel plant in one year (2018), so the model may not hold for another plant or for later years.\\n\", \"- **G.** Fitting the imputer on the training set only makes the validation results unreliable.\\n\", \"- **H.** The validation set is only two months (September and October), so the validation errors could change a lot with two other months.\\n\", \"- **I.** The test MAE proves that the model will be this accurate in every month of every year.\\n\", \"- **J.** RMSE is always smaller than MAE, so MAE is the more severe measure and should be the only one reported.\\n\", \"\\n\", \"**Next step.** Choose the one best next step:\\n\", \"- **A.** Collect readings from more years (or another plant) and check the chosen model again on months it has never seen before any decision.\\n\", \"- **B.** Move the test months into the training set so the model learns from more rows, and report the training error.\\n\", \"- **C.** Deploy the chosen model now, because the test MAE is below the client limit.\\n\", \"- **D.** Tune the maximum depth of the decision tree until its test MAE is lowest, then report that test MAE.\\n\", \"- **E.** Remove the baseline model from the report so the results look better.\\n\", \"\\n\", \"**Written answers.** Write in your own words, in full sentences.\\n\", \"- `answer_choice`: In one or two sentences: why do you recommend this model? Use a number from the validation set and say what you compared it with.\\n\", \"- `answer_test_set`: In one or two sentences: why is the test set opened only once, at the very end, and never used to choose the model?\\n\", \"\\n\", \"Each course has its own lettering of these lists.\"]}, {\"cell_type\": \"code\", \"metadata\": {\"tags\": [\"iuea-memo\"]}, \"source\": [\"#@title Part B: the decision memo form (fill in every field; do not rename a field)\\n\", \"MEMO = {\\n\",