se sqrt(2.5)\\\",\\n\", \"                    lambda: abs(regression_errors([1, 3], [2, 5])[\\\"mae\\\"] - 1.5) < 1e-9 and abs(regression_errors([1, 3], [2, 5])[\\\"rmse\\\"] - 2.5 ** 0.5) < 1e-9))\\n\", \"_checks.append(_try(\\\"classification_scores on a known case (tp 1, fp 1, fn 1, tn 1, precision 0.5, recall 0.5)\\\",\\n\", \"                    lambda: (lambda s: (s[\\\"tp\\\"], s[\\\"fp\\\"], s[\\\"fn\\\"], s[\\\"tn\\\"], s[\\\"precision\\\"], s[\\\"recall\\\"]) == (1, 1, 1, 1, 0.5, 0.5))(classification_scores([1, 0, 1, 0], [0.9, 0.8, 0.2, 0.1]))))\\n\", \"_checks.append(_try(\\\"a probability of exactly 0.5 counts as a warning\\\", lambda: classification_scores([1], [0.5])[\\\"tp\\\"] == 1))\\n\", \"_checks.append(_try(\\\"warning_probabilities gives numbers between 0 and 1\\\",\\n\", \"                    lambda: all(0 <= p <= 1 for p in warning_probabilities(_toy, _new, 8.0))))\\n\", \"for _name in [\\\"validation_mae\\\", \\\"warning_scores\\\", \\\"candidate_table\\\", \\\"chosen_model\\\"]:\\n\", \"    _checks.append(_try(\\\"the variable \\\" + _name + \\\" has been calculated (it is not None)\\\", lambda: globals().get(_name) is not None))\\n\", \"_checks.append(_try(\\\"the test set has been opened exactly once\\\", lambda: len(TEST_OPEN_LOG) == 1))\\n\", \"_checks.append(_try(\\\"Chart 1 and Chart 2 each have a title, named axes and the unit\\\",\\n\", \"                    lambda: all(f.axes[0].get_title() and f.axes[0].get_xlabel() and TARGET_UNIT.lower() in f.axes[0].get_ylabel().lower() for f in (chart_1, chart_2))))\\n\", \"print()\\n\", \"print(sum(_checks), \\\"of\\\", len(_checks), \\\"self-checks pass. Now choose Runtime, Restart session and run all, and check that nothing stops with an error.\\\")\\n\"], \"execution_count\": null, \"outputs\": []}, {\"cell_type\": \"markdown\", \"metadata\": {}, \"source\": [\"## Task 7: Part B, the decision memo form (15 automatic marks)\\n\", \"Your memo is a **form**. You write it for **the plant's energy manager**. Fill in the dictionary `MEMO` in the next cell. Every value is checked by the marking computer; nothing is read by a person. Use your own numbers, with at least two decimals, in **kVarh**.\\n\", \"\\n\", \"| Field | What to enter | Marks |\\n\", \"|---|---|---|\\n\", \"| `recommended_model` | One of the models you trained (`\\\"baseline\\\"`, `\\\"linear\\\"`, `\\\"tree\\\"`). It must be the model the supplied rule chose and the model you opened the test set with. | 3 |\\n\", \"| `validation_mae` | The validation MAE of each of the three models, as your notebook computed them. | 3 |\\n\", \"| `test_mae`, `test_recall` | The MAE and the warning recall on the test set from your ONE opening (recall is between 0 and 1). The marking computer recomputes them from your own functions. | 2 |\\n\", \"| `improvement_over_baseline` | The validation MAE of the baseline model minus the validation MAE of your recommended model, in kVarh (0 if you recommend the baseline). | 1 |\\n\", \"| `limits` | The letters of the **three** statements below that are **true limits of this study**. Three different letters. One mark for each true one. | 3 |\\n\", \"| `next_step` | One letter: the best next step. | 1 |\\n\", \"| `answer_choice`, `answer_test_set` | Two short written answers of 8 to 80 words each. One mark each. | 2 |\\n\", \"\\n\", \"**Limits.** Choose the three statements that are TRUE and are limits of this study (some statements are false):\\n\", \"- **A.** Fitting the imputer on the training set only makes the validation results unreliable.\\n\", \"- **B.** Because the test set was opened only once, the test metrics have no uncertainty at all.\\n\", \"- **C.** The test set is only November and December of the same year, so the test metrics are one estimate that may be luckier or unluckier than the truth.\\n\", \"- **D.** The client limits (the error limit and the time limit) and the warning limit are invented teaching numbers; a real client would set their own.\\n\", \"- **E.** The test MAE proves that the model will be this accurate in every month of every year.\\n\", \"- **F.** The validation set is only two months (September and October), so the validation errors could change a lot with two other months.\\n\", \"- **G.** The model with the lowest training error is always the best model for new months.\\n\", \"- **H.** The baseline model should be left out of the comparison because it uses no features.\\n\", \"- **I.** All the readings come from one steel plant in one year (2018), so the model may not hold for another plant or for later years.\\n\", \"- **J.** RMSE is always smaller than MAE, so MAE is the more severe measure and should be the only one reported.\\n\", \"\\n\", \"**Next step.** Choose the one best next step:\\n\", \"- **A.** Move the test months into the training set so the model learns from more rows, and report the training error.\\n\", \"- **B.** Remove the baseline model from the report so the results look better.\\n\", \"- **C.** Collect readings from more years (or another plant) and check the chosen model again on months it has never seen before any decision.\\n\", \"- **D.** Deploy the chosen model now, because the test MAE is below the client limit.\\n\", \"- **E.** Tune the maximum depth of the decision tree until its test MAE is lowest, then report that test MAE.\\n\", \"\\n\", \"**Written answers.** Write in your own words, in full sentences.\\n\", \"- `answer_choice`: In one or two sentences: why do you recommend this model? Use a number from the validation set and say what you compared it with.\\n\", \"- `answer_test_set`: In one or two sentences: why is the test set opened only once, at the very end, and never used to choose the model?\\n\", \"\\n\", \"Each course has its own lettering of these lists.\"]}, {\"cell_type\": \"code\", \"metadata\": {\"tags\": [\"iuea-memo\"]}, \"source\": [\"#@title Part B: the decision memo form (fill in every field; do not rename a field)\\n\", \"MEMO = {\\n\",